meta {
  name: delete session
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/{{sessionId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Delete one stored session (JSONL + blob folder). 204 success, 400 malformed id, 404 unknown.
  
  CAUTION: This really deletes the session, and it is the one destructive endpoint without an ORIGIN fence — the host fence and the id shape check are the guards, a foreign Origin from a local page is not refused here. Point it at a throwaway home before replaying the whole collection.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: yes
}
